{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "module_id": "default",
  "module_type": "default",
  "description": "Common auditable-code rules shared by all Styio-family repositories.",
  "last_updated": "2026-06-29",
  "required_audit_fields": [
    "**Severity:**",
    "**Evidence:**",
    "**Test evidence:**",
    "**Data lifecycle:**",
    "**Gate impact:**",
    "**Required closure:**"
  ],
  "required_closure_fields": [
    "**Closure evidence:**",
    "**Coverage evidence:**",
    "**Data lifecycle evidence:**",
    "**Gate evidence:**"
  ],
  "required_checklist_markers": [
    "Check The Seven Design Principles First",
    "Verify Lifecycle Test Coverage",
    "Audit Data Structures, Data Flow, And Lifecycle State Machines",
    "Optimize Delivery Gates For Quality",
    "**Data lifecycle:**",
    "**Gate impact:**"
  ],
  "audit_items": [
    "Design-principle compliance is checked before local style.",
    "Lifecycle test coverage must be proven with project tools.",
    "Every non-trivial data/resource structure must have an auditable state machine.",
    "Delivery gates are judged by quality protection, not by whether current code passes.",
    "Styio-family repositories must publish Apache-2.0 license evidence and source-distribution obligations.",
    "Styio-family repositories must reject dependencies that require commercial authorization, subscription, or membership-gated access.",
    "Every project module manifest must list its technology stack, internal components, open-source components, and dependency manifests.",
    "Every SymPolicy repository in the Styio ecosystem must have a dedicated project module directory loaded after the common default audit module.",
    "Every Styio-family repository must reject repository-junk files, temporary files, caches, build outputs, logs, raw data dumps, archives, and oversized generated artifacts before pull-request submission.",
    "SymPolicy core repositories must expose release, stable, and nightly branches before delivery can pass.",
    "SymPolicy upstream repositories must carry a repository-local styio-audit workflow that exactly matches the authoritative template shipped by styio-audit.",
    "Local upstream and downstream repositories should install the authoritative styio-audit pre-commit hook so staged secrets, IP literals, and backend infrastructure details are blocked before entering any branch.",
    "Styio compiler repositories must expose a local delivery framework whose CI, scheduler, workflow documents, and scheduler tests are externally auditable by styio-audit.",
    "SymPolicy upstream repositories must allow temporary branches to target nightly, require nightly to promote to stable, and require stable to promote to release.",
    "Unka-Malloc downstream repositories must allow temporary branches to target nightly, require nightly to promote to stable, and require stable to promote to release.",
    "Any branch other than release, stable, and nightly is a temporary branch with no special name semantics; once its pull request is merged, GitHub must delete it automatically.",
    "Styio-family repositories must not contain passwords, tokens, API keys, private keys, client secrets, or access keys in tracked source or git history.",
    "Every Styio-family repository must run the common module, inventory, resource-scope, secret, and IP exposure checks unless a policy explicitly scopes a stricter gate to a smaller business line.",
    "Backend operations repositories such as the package manager, platform service, and community service must keep official operations, cloud resource identifiers, production deployment material, and service DSNs out of public source.",
    "Open-source backend operations repositories may publish standard auth, privacy, password-storage, and key-generation implementations only when secrets and production materials stay private and dangerous security patterns are blocked.",
    "Documentation, example, benchmark, website, and development-environment repositories run the common baseline without backend operations gates unless their project module declares a backend-operations profile."
  ],
